<title>JAPAN: NKK Corp up on blast furnace resumption reports.</title>
<headline>NKK Corp up on blast furnace resumption reports.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in NKK Corp rose on Wednesday morning, spurred by reports that the steel maker plans to reopen a blast furnace to meet increasing demand for steel in Asia, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0117 GMT, the shares were up 14 yen at 245, making them the largest percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. NKK was the second most heavily traded issue, with turnover of 5.882 million shares.</p>
</text>
